+# Base USDC Yield Vault — v1
+
+An ERC-4626 vault on Base that takes USDC deposits, pairs them with WETH in Aerodrome
+liquidity, stakes the LP in the pool's gauge, and lets a keeper compound the AERO emissions
+back into the position.
+
+```
+depositor --USDC--> YieldVault (ERC-4626, shares)
+                        |  earn()            keeper
+                        v
+        AerodromeUsdcWethStrategy
+                        |  1. rebalance USDC/WETH legs to equal value (Aerodrome Router)
+                        |  2. addLiquidity -> vAMM-WETH/USDC LP
+                        |  3. Gauge.deposit(LP)
+                        v
+        harvest() (keeper): Gauge.getReward -> AERO
+                            -> performance fee to treasury
+                            -> AERO/USDC swap -> back to step 1
+```
+
+| Contract | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `src/YieldVault.sol` | ERC-4626 USDC vault: shares, deposit cap, pause, keeper `earn()`, withdrawal routing |
+| `src/AerodromeUsdcWethStrategy.sol` | Zap, staking, `harvest()`, valuation, price guards, emergency exit |
+| `src/interfaces/IAerodrome.sol` | Minimal Pool / Router / Gauge / Voter / PoolFactory interfaces |
+| `script/Deploy.s.sol` | Deployment + pre-flight checks on the live venue |
+| `script/Keeper.s.sol` | `Earn` and `Harvest` keeper entrypoints |
+
+## Build and test
+
+Dependencies (already vendored in `lib/`, re-install with):
+
+```bash
+forge install foundry-rs/forge-std OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts@v5.1.0
+```
+
+```bash
+forge build
+forge test                        # unit tests always run; fork tests need Base RPC
+BASE_RPC_URL=https://mainnet.base.org forge test -vv
+```
+
+`test/YieldVault.t.sol` (18 tests) covers vault accounting, caps, pausing, migration, the
+inflation attack and failure paths against a mock strategy — no network needed.
+`test/AerodromeStrategyFork.t.sol` (14 tests) runs the whole flow against live Base state at
+block 50,235,000. The fork suite skips itself (rather than failing) if the RPC cannot serve
+that state, so `forge test` passes offline; point `BASE_RPC_URL` at an archive node to always
+run it.
+
+## Deployment
+
+1. `cp .env.example .env` and fill in `OWNER` (multisig), `TREASURY`, `KEEPER`, `DEPOSIT_CAP`.
+2. Dry run, then broadcast:
+
+```bash
+forge script script/Deploy.s.sol:Deploy --rpc-url $BASE_RPC_URL --sender $DEPLOYER
+forge script script/Deploy.s.sol:Deploy --rpc-url $BASE_RPC_URL --broadcast --verify
+```
+
+The script refuses to deploy unless the pool exists, its gauge is alive and the gauge still
+pays AERO. It deploys the vault and strategy, wires them together, registers the keeper, and
+starts an `Ownable2Step` handover.
+
+3. **`OWNER` must call `acceptOwnership()` on both contracts** — until then the deployer is
+   still in control.
+4. Seed a small deposit (e.g. 100 USDC) yourself, call `earn()`, and confirm
+   `vault.convertToAssets(1e6)` is ~1e6 and `gauge.balanceOf(strategy) > 0` before raising
+   `depositCap` for the public.
+
+Owner-only levers after deployment: `setDepositCap`, `pause`/`unpause`, `setStrategy`,
+`setKeeper`, and on the strategy `setParams` (performance fee ≤ 20%, slippage, deviation
+guard, withdrawal buffer), `setTreasury`, `setGauge`, `panic`, `resume`, `sweep`.
+
+## Keeper operation
+
+Two jobs, both idempotent and safe to retry:
+
+```bash
+# deploy idle deposits (EARN_CHUNK caps how much is zapped per tx)
+VAULT=0x... EARN_CHUNK=100000000000 forge script script/Keeper.s.sol:Earn \
+  --rpc-url $BASE_RPC_URL --broadcast
+
+# claim + compound (skips when the pending reward is below MIN_HARVEST_USDC)
+STRATEGY=0x... MIN_HARVEST_USDC=25000000 forge script script/Keeper.s.sol:Harvest \
+  --rpc-url $BASE_RPC_URL --broadcast
+```
+
+- **Cadence.** Emissions stream per second and are claimable at any time; harvesting is purely
+  an economics question. At the emission rate measured below, a $250k position accrues roughly
+  $290/week, and a harvest costs cents on Base — once or twice a week is ample, and the
+  `MIN_HARVEST_USDC` guard stops the keeper burning gas on dust.
+- **Chunk large inflows.** `earn()` zaps through a $8.3M pool; price impact grows with size and
+  is paid out of pooled assets. Use `earn(uint256)` / `EARN_CHUNK` to split anything large
+  across several transactions or blocks.
+- **Expected reverts and the response:**
+  | Revert | Meaning | Action |
+  | --- | --- | --- |
+  | `PriceOutOfRange` | pool spot is >2% away from its 2h TWAP | wait and retry; this is the anti-manipulation guard doing its job |
+  | `InsufficientAmountA/B`, router `InsufficientOutputAmount` | price moved between simulation and inclusion | retry; if persistent, the owner can widen `slippageBps` |
+  | `GaugeNotAlive` | governance killed the gauge | owner runs `panic(minOut)`, then `setGauge(newGauge)` once a live one exists, then `resume()` |
+  | `NotKeeper` | keeper address not registered | owner calls `setKeeper` |
+- **Monitor:** `Voter.isAlive(gauge)`, `gauge.rewardRate()` (emissions can be redirected away
+  from this pool between epochs), `gauge.earned(strategy)`, `vault.convertToAssets(1e6)` as the
+  share price, and AERO landing in the treasury on each harvest.
+
+## Why these integrations
+
+All figures were read from Base mainnet at block **50,235,433 (2026-08-20 21:10 UTC)** with
+`cast`; the addresses are also the ones published in the
+[aerodrome-finance/contracts](https://github.com/aerodrome-finance/contracts) README.
+
+**Aerodrome, not Uniswap.** Aerodrome is the venue on Base where a USDC/WETH LP position earns a
+*claimable, programmatic* reward — the brief's "claim and compound" only exists if something is
+claimable. Uniswap v3/v4 positions on Base pay trading fees into an NFT position with no reward
+token to harvest, and would require range management in v1. Aerodrome is also the largest DEX on
+Base by TVL and volume.
+
+**The gauged vAMM pool, and what that implies.**
+
+| Verified onchain | Value |
+| --- | --- |
+| Pool `0xcDAC0d6c6C59727a65F871236188350531885C43` | `vAMM-WETH/USDC`, 30 bps fee (`PoolFactory.getFee`) |
+| Reserves | 1,794.97 WETH + 4,164,282 USDC ≈ **$8.33M** |
+| Gauge `0x519BBD1Dd8C6A94C46080E24f316c14Ee758C025` | `isAlive = true`, `rewardToken = AERO` |
+| Emissions | `rewardRate` 0.033929 AERO/s → **20,520 AERO/week ≈ $9.75k** → ~**6.1% APR** |
+| Staked share | 83.51M of 84.62M LP supply (**98.7%**) is in the gauge |
+| Reward exit route | `vAMM-USDC/AERO` `0x6cDcb1C4A4D1C3C6d054b27AC5B77e89eAFb971d`, 14.09M USDC / 29.63M AERO — deep enough that harvest-sized sales are noise |
+
+Two consequences we had to design around, both read from the deployed
+[`Gauge.sol`](https://github.com/aerodrome-finance/contracts/blob/main/contracts/gauges/Gauge.sol):
+
+- `Gauge._claimFees()` forwards the pool's trading fees to `feesVotingReward` — i.e. to the
+  pool's *voters*, not to staked LPs. **AERO emissions are the entire yield of this position**;
+  there are no trading fees to harvest. (Not staking would keep the 30 bps fees instead, but
+  98.7% of this pool's LPs stake, which is the market's verdict on which side pays more.)
+- `Gauge.deposit()` reverts once `Voter.isAlive(gauge)` is false. A killed gauge therefore
+  bricks compounding, which is why the strategy has `panic()` (unwind everything to USDC) and
+  `setGauge()` (re-point at the pool's current gauge, validated through the Voter).
+
+**The trade-off we accepted: vAMM over Slipstream (CL).** The concentrated-liquidity
+`CL100-WETH/USDC` pool `0xb2cc224c1c9feE385f8ad6a55b4d94E92359DC59` (gauge
+`0xF33a96b5932D9E9B9A0eDA447AbD8C9d48d2e0c8`) receives `rewardRate` 0.373534 AERO/s —
+**225,914 AERO/week ≈ $107k on ~$10.05M of liquidity, roughly 55% APR versus 6.1% here.**
+That is ~9x the emissions, and we are deliberately not taking it in v1: a CL position is an
+NFT with a price range, so the vault would need range selection, rebalancing, and per-position
+accounting, and it carries much sharper impermanent loss when price leaves the range. The vAMM
+LP is a plain fungible ERC-20 that a gauge stakes 1:1, which is what makes this version small
+enough to review. **Migrating to Slipstream is the obvious v2**, and `vault.setStrategy()`
+exists for exactly that.
+
+**On the "Predictive Allocation" news.** Aerodrome announced (2026-07-26) that Predictive
+Allocation replaces weekly veAERO gauge voting; coverage disagrees on whether it is already
+live or lands in September 2026. We did not take the announcement's word for the current state:
+at our verified block the classic mechanics are still running — `Voter.weights(pool)` is
+4.96e24 and the gauge's `periodFinish` is the next Thursday epoch flip (2026-08-27). It also
+does not change our integration surface: the strategy only ever calls `Gauge.deposit`,
+`Gauge.withdraw`, `Gauge.getReward` and reads `Voter.isAlive`. What *can* change is how much
+this pool is allocated — hence the emissions monitoring above and the ability to migrate.
+
+## Safety properties, and how they are enforced
+
+- **Share price cannot be moved by a spot-price push.** `estimatedTotalAssets()` values the LP
+  with fair reserves (`2 * sqrt(k * price)`) using the pool's own ~2h TWAP oracle
+  (`Pool.quote(token, amount, 4)`, one observation per 30-minute period), not with live
+  reserves. `test_Fork_ShareValueSurvivesSpotManipulation` dumps 400 WETH into the pool and the
+  vault's `totalAssets()` moves <0.2%.
+- **Nothing trades while the pool is manipulated.** Every zap, unwind and harvest first checks
+  spot against the TWAP and reverts with `PriceOutOfRange` beyond `maxPriceDeviationBps` (2%)
+  — see `test_Fork_SpotManipulationBlocksInvest`.
+- **Swap floors are TWAP-anchored,** not derived from same-transaction reserves (which a
+  sandwicher controls). A swap's `minOut` is the TWAP-implied amount less
+  `maxPriceDeviationBps + pool fee + slippageBps` (2% + 0.3% + 0.5% today), so worst-case
+  execution is bounded even if the keeper is compromised.
+- **Roles.** Depositors are permissionless; `earn`/`harvest` are keeper-gated; the owner (a
+  multisig, via `Ownable2Step`) holds parameters, migration and the emergency exit. A malicious
+  keeper cannot route funds anywhere — every path is hard-coded to this pool, this gauge, and
+  the vault.
+- **First-depositor inflation attack** is neutralised by 1e6 virtual shares
+  (`_decimalsOffset() = 6`); `test_InflationAttackIsNotProfitable` shows a donating attacker
+  costs the next depositor <0.1%.
+
+## Known limitations (v1)
+
+- **Impermanent loss is real.** Depositors hold half their USDC as WETH exposure; if ETH moves,
+  the USDC-denominated position underperforms simply holding USDC, and the ~6% emissions APR
+  can easily be swamped by it. This vault is not a stable-yield product.
+- **Entry costs are socialised.** Funds are zapped in `earn()`, not per deposit, so the swap fee
+  and price impact of a new entry come out of pooled assets. A same-size entry into a $50k
+  position dilutes the incumbent by <1% (`test_Fork_EntryCostOfLaterDepositIsSocialised`).
+  Batching deposits into one `earn()` and chunking large ones is the mitigation; entry/exit
+  fees are the v2 fix.
+- **Withdrawals depend on the price guard.** If spot sits >2% from the TWAP, `withdraw` from the
+  strategy reverts; the idle balance is still withdrawable, and the guard clears with normal
+  arbitrage. `panic()` is the manual override.
+- Round-trip cost (zap in, unwind out) is ~1% at current depth; the withdrawal buffer leaves
+  sub-0.1% dust in the strategy that accrues to remaining depositors.
+- `maxWithdraw`/`maxRedeem` report a holder's full balance; they do not model the exceptional
+  case where the price guard blocks strategy liquidation, so a withdrawal can revert while they
+  report a non-zero figure.
+- Single strategy, no timelock on owner actions, no ERC-4626 entry/exit fees, and the
+  contracts are **unaudited**. Keep `depositCap` small until that changes.
